apt 2.7.14 apt-pkg: force-link the debSystem instance in static builds

pkgInitSystem() picks the packaging system by scoring every entry in
pkgSystem::GlobalList, which is populated by the constructors of the
per-system global instances (debSystem debSys lives in debsystem.cc).
With a static library the linker pulls object files per referenced
symbol; nothing in libapt-pkg.a, apt-private.a or the test binary
references debsystem.cc.obj, so debSys's constructor never runs and
GlobalList stays empty.  Verified with a debug harness:

  GlobalListLen=0
  pkgInitSystem=0 Sys=0
  E: Unable to determine a suitable packaging system type

Upstream builds libapt-pkg as a shared library where every object is
present and the constructor always runs, which is why this never
surfaced on Debian.

Fix: in pkgInitSystem() take the address of the global debSys (odr-use)
under __OHOS__ so the object file is always pulled into the link and the
constructor registers the system.  In a shared-library build the same
reference is trivially satisfied and has no effect.
--- a/apt-pkg/init.cc
+++ b/apt-pkg/init.cc
@@ -15,6 +15,9 @@
 #include <apt-pkg/init.h>
 #include <apt-pkg/macros.h>
 #include <apt-pkg/pkgsystem.h>
+#ifdef __OHOS__
+#include <apt-pkg/debsystem.h>
+#endif
 #include <apt-pkg/strutl.h>
 
 #include <cstdlib>
@@ -276,6 +279,16 @@
 bool pkgInitSystem(Configuration &Cnf,pkgSystem *&Sys)
 {
    Sys = 0;
+#ifdef __OHOS__
+   // 静态库(musl/OHOS)按对象粒度裁剪链接：没有代码引用 debsystem.cc.obj 时，
+   // 全局对象 debSys 的构造器不会执行，pkgSystem::GlobalList 为空，评分循环
+   // 选不出任何系统，pkgInitSystem() 报
+   // "Unable to determine a suitable packaging system type"（libapt_test 实测
+   // GlobalListLen=0）。显式取 debSys 地址强制链接该对象，让构造器完成自注册。
+   // Debian 构建为共享库、所有对象都在 .so 里，此引用同样成立、无副作用。
+   extern debSystem debSys;
+   (void)&debSys;
+#endif
    std::string Label = Cnf.Find("Apt::System","");
    if (Label.empty() == false)
    {

